Reason for this patch: SuperOdom levels the scans with its IMU (imu_laser_R_Gravity), but it maps the scans it receives before its first IMU message without leveling them.
When such scans arrive first (e.g., livox_sim publishing before PX4's SITL IMU is up), the first one fixes the map frame to the LiDAR's pose: with a tilted LiDAR, the map and the odometry are tilted.
Change:
- featureExtraction.cpp (livoxHandler): ignore the scans received before the first IMU message (not buffered: SuperOdom drops buffered scans one per new scan, so buffering them would delay all later scans).

diff --git a/super_odometry/src/FeatureExtraction/featureExtraction.cpp b/super_odometry/src/FeatureExtraction/featureExtraction.cpp
index a6dd44d..1ecf9bc 100755
--- a/super_odometry/src/FeatureExtraction/featureExtraction.cpp
+++ b/super_odometry/src/FeatureExtraction/featureExtraction.cpp
@@ -782,6 +782,7 @@ namespace super_odometry {
             return; 
 
         m_buf.lock();
+        if (imuBuf.empty()) { m_buf.unlock(); return; } // Ignore scans until the first IMU message
         
         pcl::PointCloud<point_os::PointcloudXYZITR>::Ptr pointCloud(
             new pcl::PointCloud<point_os::PointcloudXYZITR>());
